.TH SDL_ReadIO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ReadIO \- Read from a data source.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_ReadIO(SDL_IOStream *context, void *ptr, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function reads up
.BR size
bytes from the data source to the area pointed at by
.BR ptr \[char46]
This function may read less bytes than requested\[char46]
.PP
This function will return zero when the data stream is completely read, and
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return
.BR SDL_IO_STATUS_EOF \[char46]
If zero is returned and the stream is not at EOF,
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return a different error value and
.BR SDL_GetError ()
will offer a human-readable message\[char46]
.PP
A request for zero bytes on a valid stream will return zero immediately without accessing the stream, so the stream status (EOF, err, etc) will not change\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I context
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure\[char46]
.TP
.I ptr
a pointer to a buffer to read data into\[char46]
.TP
.I size
the number of bytes to read from the data source\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes read, or 0 on end of file or other failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_WriteIO (3),
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus (3)
